From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:30:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add native harness conversation history seeding

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: seed durable harness sessions from prior conversation turns
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add the native jcode harness API and daemon support needed for a caller to seed
an ordinary session transcript with ordered plain-text user and assistant turns
before receiving the normal Attached response.

Why it exists:
The standalone evaluator client is maintained directly in the catalog, while
jcode product code needs a supported protocol path to persist imported turns.
The daemon validates roles, content, counts, and UTF-8 byte limits, writes one
atomic batch, exposes provider-visible messages, and rolls back failed creates.

Upstream integration points:
Extend crates/jcode-harness-api request and error schemas, the native
jcode-protocol request/event wire, the harness API bridge translation state, and
jcode-app-core Agent/session lifecycle handling. Existing Subscribe, Session,
Agent, GetHistory, and Pong capability paths remain the compatibility anchors.

Update guidance:
Keep the daemon session_initial_history capability probe and API initial_history
advertisement synchronized. Preserve correlated seed completion before Attached,
normal User/Assistant stored messages, no model-turn events during seeding, and
rollback of failed fresh sessions. Keep empty-history create behavior unchanged.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-harness-api -p jcode-protocol -p jcode-harness-api-server --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib server::client_lifecycle:: -- --test-threads=1
cargo test -p jcode-sdk --test client_behavior session_busy_protocol_error_has_a_stable_sdk_code
